source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"VCC : C1.1(passive) J5.2(Pin_2,passive) JP1.2(B,passive) Q1.2(S,passive) R1.1(passive) R6.1(passive) U1.3(VI,power_in)\"}], \"impact\": \"If both are fitted, outputs of the two MCUs would fight on shared pins, causing erratic PWM and tach behaviour and possible overcurrent. If they are alternates, this is an intended option and not a fault.\", \"confidence\": 0.2}], \"summary\": \"The netlist is mostly consistent (ISP header, MCU pinouts, PMOS high-side switch and tach/pull-up networks check out), but R5 is a 1 MOhm part in the fan PWM path, which would prevent the MCU from effectively driving the fan's PWM input. Lower confidence is given to the duplicated U2/U3 MCU footprints, which may be intentional alternates.\"}",
